# The 29 study frames are held back from git on purpose.
#
# They are screenshots of somebody else's product, and this repository is
# public. Committing them is easy and undoing it is not, so the decision is
# the owner's — see the note in README.md. The frames exist on disk in the
# session that made them, and `../extract-frames.py` regenerates them from
# the recordings in seconds.
*.jpg
